* === 2. TRANSMISSION CHANNEL: CHAOTIC MASKING SUMMER ===
* Transmitted Signal: S_chan = V(Vc1_tx) + V(msg)
SYMBOL bv 1100 80 R0
SYMATTR InstName B_chan
SYMATTR Value V=V(Vc1_tx)+V(msg)
WIRE 1100 96 1100 50
FLAG 1100 50 S_chan
WIRE 1100 176 1100 210
FLAG 1100 210 0

* === 3. SYNCHRONIZATION COUPLING ===
* Coupling resistor Rc = 270 ohms injects S_chan into receiver Vc1_rx
WIRE 1100 50 1150 50
FLAG 1150 50 S_chan
SYMBOL res 200 470 R0
SYMATTR InstName R_couple
SYMATTR Value 270
WIRE 216 486 216 450
FLAG 216 450 S_chan
WIRE 216 566 216 600
FLAG 216 600 Vc1_rx

* === 4. RECEIVER MESSAGE DECRYPTION & RECONSTRUCTION ===
* Subtraction Stage: V(msg_raw) = V(S_chan) - V(Vc1_rx)
SYMBOL bv 1100 500 R0
SYMATTR InstName B_sub
SYMATTR Value V=V(S_chan)-V(Vc1_rx)
WIRE 1100 516 1100 470
FLAG 1100 470 msg_raw
WIRE 1100 596 1100 630
FLAG 1100 630 0

* Reconstruction Low-Pass Filter (R_filt = 10k, C_filt = 6.8n -> Cutoff ~ 2.3 kHz)
